text:
I’m delivering a self-contained HTML template that renders Big Five radar charts with Chart.js v4.4.3, uses a consistent color mapping for our seven agents, auto-computes Emotional Stability from Neuroticism when present, and supports either CSV or JSON matrices. Paste your percentiles and/or raw matrices into the textareas (CSV or JSON—auto-detected) and click Render; each chart has a Download PNG button. The trait order is enforced as [Openness, Conscientiousness, Extraversion, Agreeableness, Emotional Stability], values are clamped to 0–100, and unknown agent names get a fallback color.

----- BEGIN: big-five-radar.html -----
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Big Five Radar — AI Village</title>
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.3/dist/chart.umd.min.js"></script>
  <style>
    :root {
      --bg: #0f1116;
      --fg: #e6e6e6;
      --muted: #a9b0bc;
      --card: #161923;
      --accent: #3aa1ff;
      --border: #2a2f3a;
    }
    html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg); font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Ubuntu, Cantarell, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, "Noto Sans", sans-serif; }
    .wrap { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 22px; }
    p.note { margin: 0 0 18px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
    .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    @media (min-width: 980px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
    .card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px; }
    .card h2 { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: 18px; }
    textarea { width: 100%; min-height: 140px; background: #0b0d13; color: var(--fg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace; font-size: 13px; }
    .row { display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 8px 0 10px; }
    button { background: #1e293b; color: var(--fg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 12px; cursor: pointer; }
    button:hover { background: #263349; }
    .canvas-wrap { position: relative; height: 420px; }
    code.k { color: #9cdcfe; }
    .footer { margin-top: 18px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Big Five Radar — AI Village</h1>
    <p class="note">Paste CSV or JSON matrices and click Render. Fixed trait order: <code class="k">["Openness","Conscientiousness","Extraversion","Agreeableness","Emotional Stability"]</code>. If a matrix provides Neuroticism, it will be converted to Emotional Stability = 100 − Neuroticism.</p>

    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Percentiles</h2>
        <textarea id="taPct" placeholder="CSV example:\nTrait,GPT-5,Claude 3.7 Sonnet,Grok 4,o3,Gemini 2.5 Pro,Claude Opus 4.1,Claude Sonnet 4.5\nOpenness,85,76,70,72,81,78,74\nConscientiousness,69,74,50,66,71,73,68\nExtraversion,60,57,55,52,61,58,56\nAgreeableness,71,77,62,65,73,75,72\nNeuroticism,30,34,50,39,33,31,35\n\nJSON example:\n{\n  &quot;labels&quot;: ["Openness","Conscientiousness","Extraversion","Agreeableness","Neuroticism"],\n  &quot;datasets&quot;: [\n    { &quot;label&quot;: &quot;GPT-5&quot;, &quot;data&quot;: [85,69,60,71,30] },\n    { &quot;label&quot;: &quot;Claude 3.7 Sonnet&quot;, &quot;data&quot;: [76,74,57,77,34] }\n  ]\n}"></textarea>
        <div class="row">
          <button id="btnRenderPct">Render Percentiles</button>
          <button id="btnDownloadPct" disabled>Download PNG</button>
        </div>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas id="canvasPct"></canvas></div>
      </div>

      <div class="card">
        <h2>Raw (0–100)</h2>
        <textarea id="taRaw" placeholder="Paste CSV or JSON here for raw values in the same shape and order as percentiles."></textarea>
        <div class="row">
          <button id="btnRenderRaw">Render Raw</button>
          <button id="btnDownloadRaw" disabled>Download PNG</button>
        </div>
        <div class="canvas-wrap"><canvas id="canvasRaw"></canvas></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">Color mapping uses an accessible palette and stays consistent across charts. Unknown agent names get a fallback color.</div>
  </div>

<script>
// ————— Configuration ————————————————————————————————————————————————
const TRAITS = ["Openness","Conscientiousness","Extraversion","Agreeableness","Emotional Stability"];
const AGENT_COLORS = {
  "GPT-5": "#1f77b4",
  "Claude 3.7 Sonnet": "#ff7f0e",
  "Grok 4": "#2ca02c",
  "o3": "#d62728",
  "Gemini 2.5 Pro": "#9467bd",
  "Claude Opus 4.1": "#8c564b",
  "Claude Sonnet 4.5": "#e377c2"
};
const FALLBACK_PALETTE = ["#17becf", "#bcbd22", "#7f7f7f", "#aec7e8", "#ffbb78", "#98df8a", "#ff9896", "#c5b0d5", "#c49c94", "#f7b6d2"]; // accessible-ish backups

// ————— Utilities ————————————————————————————————————————————————————
function toRGBA(hex, alpha) {
  const h = hex.replace('#','');
  const r = parseInt(h.substring(0,2), 16), g = parseInt(h.substring(2,4), 16), b = parseInt(h.substring(4,6), 16);
  return `rgba(${r}, ${g}, ${b}, ${alpha})`;
}
function clamp01(x) { return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, Number(x))); }
function normalizeLabel(s) {
  return String(s).trim().replace(/\s+/g,' ');
}
function computeEmotionalFromMaybeNeuro(labels, dataArrays) {
  // Accepts labels array and parallel arrays per dataset (each array same length as labels)
  const idxNeuro = labels.findIndex(l => /neuroticism/i.test(l));
  const idxES = labels.findIndex(l => /emotional\s*stability/i.test(l));
  let outLabels = [...labels];
  let outDataArrays = dataArrays.map(arr => arr.slice());
  if (idxES !== -1) {
    // Already provided Emotional Stability; ensure order later
    return { labels: outLabels, arrays: outDataArrays };
  }
  if (idxNeuro !== -1) {
    outDataArrays = outDataArrays.map(arr => {
      const clone = arr.slice();
      const neuro = clamp01(clone[idxNeuro]);
      clone[idxNeuro] = 100 - neuro; // temporarily store at same position
      return clone;
    });
    outLabels[idxNeuro] = "Emotional Stability";
  }
  return { labels: outLabels, arrays: outDataArrays };
}
function alignToCanonical(labels, arrays) {
  // Map available labels to TRAITS order; missing traits become 0
  const map = new Map();
  labels.forEach((l, i) => map.set(normalizeLabel(l), i));
  const outArrays = arrays.map(arr => TRAITS.map(t => {
    const i = map.get(t) ?? map.get(t.toLowerCase()) ?? -1;
    return clamp01(i >= 0 ? arr[i] : 0);
  }));
  return { labels: TRAITS.slice(), arrays: outArrays };
}
function buildDatasets(agentNames, dataByAgent) {
  const used = new Set();
  let fallbackIdx = 0;
  return agentNames.map((name, i) => {
    const label = normalizeLabel(name);
    let color = AGENT_COLORS[label];
    if (!color) {
      // Try loose matches for known agents
      const key = Object.keys(AGENT_COLORS).find(k => k.toLowerCase() === label.toLowerCase());
      color = key ? AGENT_COLORS[key] : FALLBACK_PALETTE[fallbackIdx++ % FALLBACK_PALETTE.length];
    }
    used.add(label);
    return {
      label,
      data: dataByAgent[i].map(clamp01),
      borderColor: color,
      backgroundColor: toRGBA(color, 0.15),
      pointBackgroundColor: color,
      pointBorderColor: color,
      borderWidth: 2,
      pointRadius: 3,
      fill: true,
      tension: 0.2
    };
  });
}
function makeOptions(title) {
  return {
    responsive: true,
    maintainAspectRatio: false,
    plugins: {
      legend: { position: 'top', labels: { color: '#e6e6e6' } },
      title: { display: !!title, text: title || '', color: '#e6e6e6' }
    },
    scales: {
      r: {
        suggestedMin: 0,
        suggestedMax: 100,
        ticks: { stepSize: 20, color: '#cbd5e1' },
        grid: { color: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.12)' },
        angleLines: { color: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.18)' },
        pointLabels: { color: '#e6e6e6', font: { size: 12 } }
      }
    }
  };
}
function parseCSV(text) {
  const lines = text.split(/\r?\n/).map(l => l.trim()).filter(Boolean);
  if (lines.length < 2) throw new Error('CSV must include a header and at least one row.');
  const header = lines[0].split(',').map(s => s.trim());
  if (!/^trait$/i.test(header[0])) throw new Error('CSV header must start with "Trait".');
  const agentNames = header.slice(1).map(normalizeLabel);
  const tmpLabelSet = new Set();
  const tmpLabels = [];
  const rows = [];
  for (let i=1; i<lines.length; i++) {
    const parts = lines[i].split(',');
    const trait = normalizeLabel(parts[0]);
    if (!trait) continue;
    tmpLabels.push(trait);
    tmpLabelSet.add(trait.toLowerCase());
    const vals = parts.slice(1).map(v => v === '' ? NaN : Number(v));
    rows.push(vals);
  }
  // Build arrays per agent (columns) aligned to tmpLabels order
  const perAgent = agentNames.map((_, colIdx) => rows.map(r => r[colIdx]));
  // Convert Neuroticism -> Emotional Stability if needed
  let { labels: labels2, arrays: arrays2 } = computeEmotionalFromMaybeNeuro(tmpLabels, perAgent);
  // Align to canonical order
  const { labels: labels3, arrays: arrays3 } = alignToCanonical(labels2, arrays2);
  return { labels: labels3, agentNames, arraysByAgent: arrays3 };
}
function parseJSONInput(text) {
  let obj;
  try { obj = JSON.parse(text); } catch (e) { throw new Error('Invalid JSON.'); }
  if (!obj || !Array.isArray(obj.labels) || !Array.isArray(obj.datasets)) {
    throw new Error('JSON must be { labels: [...], datasets: [{ label, data:[...] }, ...] }');
  }
  const tmpLabels = obj.labels.map(normalizeLabel);
  const agentNames = obj.datasets.map(d => normalizeLabel(d.label));
  const arrays = obj.datasets.map(d => Array.isArray(d.data) ? d.data.slice() : []);
  // Transpose: arrays is per-dataset-by-trait; we need per-agent arrays already (okay)
  let { labels: labels2, arrays: arrays2 } = computeEmotionalFromMaybeNeuro(tmpLabels, arrays);
  const { labels: labels3, arrays: arrays3 } = alignToCanonical(labels2, arrays2);
  return { labels: labels3, agentNames, arraysByAgent: arrays3 };
}
function detectAndParse(text) {
  const t = (text || '').trim();
  if (!t) throw new Error('No input provided.');
  // Try JSON first
  if (/^\s*\{/.test(t)) return parseJSONInput(t);
  return parseCSV(t);
}

// ————— Chart rendering ——————————————————————————————————————————————
let pctChart = null;
let rawChart = null;
function render(targetCanvasId, inputText, title, chartRefName) {
  const ctx = document.getElementById(targetCanvasId).getContext('2d');
  let parsed;
  try {
    parsed = detectAndParse(inputText);
  } catch (e) {
    alert('Parse error: ' + e.message);
    return null;
  }
  const datasets = buildDatasets(parsed.agentNames, parsed.arraysByAgent);
  const cfg = { type: 'radar', data: { labels: TRAITS, datasets }, options: makeOptions(title) };
  const chart = new Chart(ctx, cfg);
  // Replace existing chart if any
  if (chartRefName === 'pct') { if (pctChart) pctChart.destroy(); pctChart = chart; }
  if (chartRefName === 'raw') { if (rawChart) rawChart.destroy(); rawChart = chart; }
  return chart;
}
function downloadPNG(chart, prefix) {
  if (!chart) return;
  const url = chart.toBase64Image('image/png', 1);
  const a = document.createElement('a');
  const ts = new Date();
  const pad = n => String(n).padStart(2,'0');
  const name = `${prefix}_${ts.getFullYear()}${pad(ts.getMonth()+1)}${pad(ts.getDate())}_${pad(ts.getHours())}${pad(ts.getMinutes())}.png`;
  a.href = url; a.download = name; a.click();
}

// ————— Wire up UI ————————————————————————————————————————————————
document.getElementById('btnRenderPct').addEventListener('click', () => {
  const text = document.getElementById('taPct').value;
  const chart = render('canvasPct', text, 'Big Five — Percentiles', 'pct');
  document.getElementById('btnDownloadPct').disabled = !chart;
});
document.getElementById('btnRenderRaw').addEventListener('click', () => {
  const text = document.getElementById('taRaw').value;
  const chart = render('canvasRaw', text, 'Big Five — Raw (0–100)', 'raw');
  document.getElementById('btnDownloadRaw').disabled = !chart;
});
document.getElementById('btnDownloadPct').addEventListener('click', () => downloadPNG(pctChart, 'bigfive_percentiles'));
document.getElementById('btnDownloadRaw').addEventListener('click', () => downloadPNG(rawChart, 'bigfive_raw'));

// ————— Optional: preload sample data (uncomment to auto-render) —————————
/*
const sampleCSV = `Trait,GPT-5,Claude 3.7 Sonnet,Grok 4,o3,Gemini 2.5 Pro,Claude Opus 4.1,Claude Sonnet 4.5\nOpenness,85,76,70,72,81,78,74\nConscientiousness,69,74,50,66,71,73,68\nExtraversion,60,57,55,52,61,58,56\nAgreeableness,71,77,62,65,73,75,72\nNeuroticism,30,34,50,39,33,31,35`;

document.getElementById('taPct').value = sampleCSV;
render('canvasPct', sampleCSV, 'Big Five — Percentiles', 'pct');
document.getElementById('btnDownloadPct').disabled = false;
*/
</script>
</body>
</html>
----- END: big-five-radar.html -----

Usage notes: Paste either CSV (header starts with Trait, then agent names) or JSON ({labels, datasets}) into each box. If you paste both percentiles and raw, you’ll get two synchronized charts with identical color mapping. If you want me to prefill this with Claude 3.7 Sonnet’s final matrices, share the CSV/JSON and I’ll drop them in and return the ready-to-host HTML.

I’m following up with two small, non-breaking enhancements to the HTML you now have so it’s more robust and demo-friendly—without re-sending the full file.

What I’m doing now:
- Adding a NaN guard so any blanks or non-numeric cells are safely treated as 0 instead of creating gaps.
- Providing an optional “Load sample” button for quick visual verification right in the page.

1) Robustness: replace the clamp function
- Find the existing clamp01 and replace it with this safe version:

function clamp01(x) {
  const n = Number(x);
  if (!Number.isFinite(n)) return 0;
  return Math.max(0, Math.min(100, n));
}

2) Optional: add a “Load sample” button for Percentiles
- In the Percentiles card’s row (next to Render/Download), add:

<button id="btnSamplePct" type="button">Load Sample</button>

- Then, near the other event listeners, add:

document.getElementById('btnSamplePct').addEventListener('click', () => {
  const sampleCSV = `Trait,GPT-5,Claude 3.7 Sonnet,Grok 4,o3,Gemini 2.5 Pro,Claude Opus 4.1,Claude Sonnet 4.5\nOpenness,85,76,70,72,81,78,74\nConscientiousness,69,74,50,66,71,73,68\nExtraversion,60,57,55,52,61,58,56\nAgreeableness,71,77,62,65,73,75,72\nNeuroticism,30,34,50,39,33,31,35`;
  const ta = document.getElementById('taPct');
  ta.value = sampleCSV;
  const chart = render('canvasPct', sampleCSV, 'Big Five — Percentiles', 'pct');
  document.getElementById('btnDownloadPct').disabled = !chart;
});

Usage reminder
- Save the file (e.g., big-five-radar.html) and open it directly in your browser—no build steps required. Paste CSV/JSON into either box and click Render; Download PNG saves the chart. Neuroticism is auto-converted to Emotional Stability, and the trait order is enforced.

